{"title":"Career Roadmap · Civil Services Aspirant Roles","role":"Civil Services Aspirant Roles","summary":"Anthropology is particularly relevant to students targeting UPSC Civil Services Examination (CSE) and other competitive government examinations because Anthropology is an optional subject in the UPSC CSE Main Examination. However, the degree itself does not create a separate “Anthropology Civil Service” post. The career pathway is through competitive examinations and the specific service/post secured.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Anthropology"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Eligibility, examination pattern and service allocation can change. Always verify the latest UPSC notification before applying."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons: 2026–2046","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Anthropology + general studies foundation"}],[{"text":"2030–2032"},{"text":"Dedicated UPSC/PSC preparation"}],[{"text":"2032–2035"},{"text":"Civil-services examination + interview preparation"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Probation/training + early government service"}],[{"text":"2040–2043"},{"text":"Administrative/departmental responsibility"}],[{"text":"2043–2046"},{"text":"Senior administrative, policy or specialist responsibilities"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The actual timeline depends on the student's graduation year, examination attempts and selection."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anthropology foundation"},{"text":"Human evolution, society, culture"},{"text":"Anthropology notes"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Indian anthropology + social sciences"},{"text":"Tribal studies, caste, kinship, institutions"},{"text":"Fieldwork project"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"UPSC foundation"},{"text":"Polity, history, geography, economy"},{"text":"GS notes + mock tests"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Examination readiness"},{"text":"Optional + GS + answer writing"},{"text":"Full-length mock portfolio"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"If the B.Sc. is a 3-year program, compress the Year 4 preparation into Year 3."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Anthropology Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong conceptual knowledge."},{"type":"h","text":"Physical/Biological Anthropology"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human evolution"},{"text":"Primates"},{"text":"Human variation"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Human biology"},{"text":"Fossil evidence"},{"text":"Adaptation"},{"text":"Population studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Evolution","adaptation","variation","population"]}]},{"heading":"Cultural Anthropology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Society"},{"text":"Socialisation"},{"text":"Customs"},{"text":"Beliefs"},{"text":"Religion"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Political organisation"},{"text":"Social institutions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how anthropologists study communities and social systems."}]},{"heading":"Archaeological Anthropology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop basic knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prehistory"},{"text":"Stone Age"},{"text":"Archaeological evidence"},{"text":"Material culture"},{"text":"Early human settlements"},{"text":"Cultural evolution"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Connect archaeological evidence with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human evolution"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Social organisation"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Indian Anthropology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is especially useful for competitive-examination preparation."},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Indian society"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Caste"},{"text":"Tribe"},{"text":"Family"},{"text":"Kinship"},{"text":"Religion"},{"text":"Rural society"},{"text":"Urbanisation"},{"text":"Social change"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tribal communities"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal social organisation"},{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Land and forest issues"},{"text":"Tribal development"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Displacement"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Cultural change"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid simplistic stereotypes about tribal communities; use evidence-based anthropological perspectives."}]},{"heading":"Anthropology as UPSC Optional","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anthropology can be selected as the optional subject for UPSC CSE Mains."},{"type":"p","text":"The student should not choose it merely because the degree is Anthropology."},{"type":"p","text":"Compare:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Personal interest"},{"text":"Syllabus size"},{"text":"Previous academic background"},{"text":"Availability of study material"},{"text":"Ability to write analytical answers"},{"text":"Previous-year question patterns"},{"text":"Mock-test performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Anthropology preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Definitions"},{"text":"Thinkers"},{"text":"Theories"},{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Indian examples"},{"text":"Diagrams"},{"text":"Flowcharts"},{"text":"Current-affairs connections"}]}]},{"heading":"UPSC General Studies Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anthropology students must also develop broad knowledge beyond their degree."},{"type":"h","text":"GS Paper I"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian history"},{"text":"World history"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Indian society"},{"text":"Culture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GS Paper II"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Constitution"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Polity"},{"text":"Social justice"},{"text":"International relations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GS Paper III"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Science & technology"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Disaster management"},{"text":"Internal security"}]},{"type":"h","text":"GS Paper IV"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Integrity"},{"text":"Aptitude"},{"text":"Emotional intelligence"},{"text":"Case studies"}]}]},{"heading":"Current Affairs","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A civil-services aspirant needs a structured current-affairs system."},{"type":"p","text":"Follow:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Government policies"},{"text":"Parliament"},{"text":"Supreme Court developments"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Science & technology"},{"text":"Social issues"},{"text":"Agriculture"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Tribal affairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Avoid"},{"type":"p","text":"Collecting dozens of current-affairs PDFs without revision."},{"type":"p","text":"Instead:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Read","Analyse","Make short notes","Revise","Use in answers"]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 — Start Serious Examination Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build the examination cycle."},{"type":"flow","items":["UPSC Preparation","NCERT / Foundation","Standard Sources","Current Affairs","Prelims MCQs","Mains Answer Writing","Essay","Optional","Interview"]}]},{"heading":"Prelims Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"General Studies Paper I"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"History"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Polity"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Science & technology"},{"text":"Current affairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"CSAT"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not ignore CSAT."},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reading comprehension"},{"text":"Logical reasoning"},{"text":"Basic numeracy"},{"text":"Data interpretation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Even strong academic students should periodically test their CSAT performance."}]},{"heading":"Mains Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to write:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Introduction","Analysis","Evidence","Examples","Way forward","Conclusion"]},{"type":"h","text":"Practice"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"150-word answers"},{"text":"250-word answers"},{"text":"Timed writing"},{"text":"Previous-year questions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Structure"},{"text":"Relevance"},{"text":"Analysis"},{"text":"Examples"},{"text":"Diagrams where useful"},{"text":"Concise conclusions"}]}]},{"heading":"Essay Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anthropology can provide useful perspectives for essays involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal development"},{"text":"Culture"},{"text":"Technology"},{"text":"Social change"},{"text":"Inequality"},{"text":"Human development"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Globalisation"},{"text":"Diversity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"But essays should incorporate multiple perspectives, not only anthropology."}]},{"heading":"Anthropology Optional — Skill Engine","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","What to build"],"rows":[[{"text":"Physical anthropology"},{"text":"Human evolution + genetics"}],[{"text":"Archaeology"},{"text":"Prehistory + material culture"}],[{"text":"Social anthropology"},{"text":"Culture + institutions"}],[{"text":"Theories"},{"text":"Major anthropologists + schools"}],[{"text":"Indian anthropology"},{"text":"Tribes + caste + social change"}],[{"text":"Thinkers"},{"text":"Concept + contribution"}],[{"text":"Diagrams"},{"text":"Evolution, kinship, population"}],[{"text":"Case studies"},{"text":"Indian field examples"}],[{"text":"Current affairs"},{"text":"Connect contemporary issues"}],[{"text":"Answer writing"},{"text":"PYQs + timed answers"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships / Field Experience","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Unlike technical careers, UPSC selection does not require a conventional internship."},{"type":"p","text":"However, anthropology students can strengthen their understanding through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"University fieldwork"},{"text":"Tribal/community studies"},{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Rural-development projects"},{"text":"Social research"},{"text":"Public-policy projects"},{"text":"Government programme studies"},{"text":"Research assistantships"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong fieldwork project"},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a structured academic study of a community or social issue."},{"type":"p","text":"Possible topics:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Rural livelihoods"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Healthcare access"},{"text":"Digital adoption"},{"text":"Tribal development"},{"text":"Women's economic participation"},{"text":"Urbanisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Follow proper research ethics and obtain consent where required."}]},{"heading":"Strong Portfolio Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"Project","text":"Anthropological Study of Rural/Tribal Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Community","Livelihood","Education","Healthcare","Government Schemes","Social Change"]},{"type":"p","text":"Collect appropriately anonymised data through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Secondary research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Produce:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Methodology"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"Government-scheme mapping"},{"text":"Policy recommendations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This helps develop both anthropological thinking and policy-analysis skills."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certificates are not required for UPSC selection."},{"type":"p","text":"More useful areas are:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Indian Constitution"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"Data interpretation"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Research methodology"},{"text":"Geographic information systems"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Development studies"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Environmental studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn basic:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Data visualisation"},{"text":"Basic statistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are useful for future administrative and policy work."}]},{"heading":"Career Paths Through Civil Services","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"If selected through UPSC CSE, possible services include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Service","Broad work"],"rows":[[{"text":"IAS"},{"text":"Administration, policy implementation, district/state/national governance"}],[{"text":"IPS"},{"text":"Police administration and internal security"}],[{"text":"Indian Foreign Service"},{"text":"Diplomacy and international relations"}],[{"text":"IRS"},{"text":"Tax administration"}],[{"text":"Indian Audit & Accounts Service"},{"text":"Public financial accountability"}],[{"text":"Indian Railway Management Service"},{"text":"Railway administration/management"}],[{"text":"Other Group A/B services"},{"text":"Specialised public administration"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact services available, vacancies and allocation rules depend on the relevant examination cycle."}]},{"heading":"IAS Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A possible progression:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Anthropology","UPSC CSE","IAS Training","Assistant Collector / Sub-Divisional Administration","District-level responsibilities","District Collector / Senior Administrative Roles","State Secretariat / Central Government","Senior Administrative Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"The actual sequence and titles depend on cadre, posting and government requirements."}]},{"heading":"Anthropology + Administration","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Anthropology can provide useful perspectives for administrators working on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal welfare"},{"text":"Rural development"},{"text":"Public health"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Social justice"},{"text":"Women's development"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Poverty"},{"text":"Cultural preservation"},{"text":"Community participation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The key advantage is learning to understand why policies may succeed in one community but fail in another."}]},{"heading":"State Public Service Commission Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students who do not target UPSC exclusively can prepare for their State Public Service Commission examination."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential positions vary by state and recruitment cycle."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Deputy Collector-type administrative roles"},{"text":"Revenue administration"},{"text":"Municipal administration"},{"text":"Development administration"},{"text":"Other Group A/B positions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a student in Telangana, for example, relevant state-level recruitment should be checked against the current Telangana Public Service Commission notifications rather than relying on old eligibility rules."}]},{"heading":"Other Government Examination Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Anthropology graduate can also consider:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SSC examinations"},{"text":"Banking examinations"},{"text":"Railways"},{"text":"Insurance examinations"},{"text":"Defence examinations where eligible"},{"text":"State government examinations"},{"text":"Research/project recruitment"},{"text":"Government programme positions"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The specific eligibility depends on the individual notification."}]},{"heading":"Civil Services Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to discuss:"},{"type":"h","text":"Anthropology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why did you study Anthropology?"},{"text":"Why did you choose Anthropology as an optional?"},{"text":"What can anthropology contribute to governance?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Society"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Caste"},{"text":"Tribes"},{"text":"Urbanisation"},{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Gender"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Health"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Current affairs"},{"type":"p","text":"Be prepared to discuss issues from multiple perspectives:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Social","Economic","Political","Ethical","Administrative"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Personality Development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Civil services interviews evaluate more than factual knowledge."},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clear communication"},{"text":"Listening"},{"text":"Balanced opinions"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"},{"text":"Emotional stability"},{"text":"Ethical reasoning"},{"text":"Decision-making"},{"text":"Awareness of society"},{"text":"Intellectual curiosity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Avoid"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Extreme opinions"},{"text":"Memorised speeches"},{"text":"Overconfidence"},{"text":"Unsupported claims"},{"text":"Treating every problem as having a single solution"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A PG degree is not mandatory for UPSC CSE, because the examination requires a recognised bachelor's degree subject to the applicable notification."},{"type":"p","text":"However, PG study can be valuable for academic and specialist careers."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant programs"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.A. Anthropology"},{"text":"M.Sc. Anthropology"},{"text":"M.A. Sociology"},{"text":"M.A. Public Policy"},{"text":"M.A. Development Studies"},{"text":"M.A. Social Work"},{"text":"M.A. Political Science"},{"text":"M.A. Economics"},{"text":"M.A. Rural Development"},{"text":"M.A. Tribal Studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Choose PG study if it genuinely supports the intended career rather than delaying examination preparation without a clear reason."}]},{"heading":"Research Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students who enjoy Anthropology itself can pursue:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Anthropology","M.A./M.Sc. Anthropology","Research Assistant","PhD","Assistant Professor / Researcher","Senior Researcher / Academic"]},{"type":"h","text":"Research areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tribal studies"},{"text":"Human evolution"},{"text":"Medical anthropology"},{"text":"Forensic anthropology"},{"text":"Biological anthropology"},{"text":"Urban anthropology"},{"text":"Development anthropology"},{"text":"Environmental anthropology"},{"text":"Digital anthropology"}]}]},{"heading":"Policy & Development Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An alternative to civil services is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc. Anthropology","Development / Policy Internship","Research Assistant","Policy Analyst","Senior Policy Analyst","Programme Manager","Policy / Development Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant employers can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Think tanks"},{"text":"Development organisations"},{"text":"Research institutes"},{"text":"International development organisations"},{"text":"Government-funded programmes"},{"text":"Social-impact organisations"}]}]},{"heading":"Anthropology + Data","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Modern social research increasingly combines anthropology with quantitative and digital methods."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SPSS"},{"text":"R"},{"text":"Python basics"},{"text":"Survey design"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use data to study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Migration"},{"text":"Demographics"},{"text":"Health"},{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Livelihoods"},{"text":"Urbanisation"},{"text":"Social inequality"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a stronger qualitative + quantitative researcher profile."}]},{"heading":"AI + Anthropology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will create new research areas such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital anthropology"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction"},{"text":"Algorithmic bias"},{"text":"Online communities"},{"text":"Digital inequality"},{"text":"AI and cultural change"},{"text":"Technology adoption"},{"text":"AI's impact on employment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A future administrator or policy professional should understand not only what technology can do, but also how different communities experience it."}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Public administration is likely to become increasingly data-driven."},{"type":"p","text":"Future administrators may work with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted policy analysis"},{"text":"GIS-based governance"},{"text":"Digital public infrastructure"},{"text":"Predictive analytics"},{"text":"Real-time dashboards"},{"text":"Citizen-service platforms"},{"text":"Digital identity systems"},{"text":"Automated government workflows"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Anthropology remains relevant because technology cannot eliminate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["culture","social behaviour","institutions","community trust."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile becomes:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anthropology","Public Policy","Data","Technology","Governance"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Anthropology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physical anthropology"},{"text":"Cultural anthropology"},{"text":"Social anthropology"},{"text":"Archaeological anthropology"},{"text":"Indian anthropology"},{"text":"Tribal studies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"UPSC"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Polity"},{"text":"History"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"Economy"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Science & technology"},{"text":"Ethics"},{"text":"Current affairs"},{"text":"Essay writing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Examination Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prelims MCQs"},{"text":"Mains answer writing"},{"text":"Anthropology optional"},{"text":"Essay"},{"text":"Interview"},{"text":"Revision systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Governance"},{"text":"Ethical reasoning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic Python"},{"text":"Data visualisation"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Anthropology fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Indian anthropology + fieldwork"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"GS foundation + optional preparation"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Full UPSC preparation + answer writing"}],[{"text":"0–2 years after UG"},{"text":"UPSC/State PSC examination cycle"}],[{"text":"After selection"},{"text":"Foundation/professional training"}],[{"text":"Early career"},{"text":"Field administration / departmental role"}],[{"text":"5–10 years"},{"text":"Senior administrative responsibilities"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"State/Central policy and leadership roles"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate targeting Civil Services Aspirant Roles should have:"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Sc. Anthropology + strong anthropology fundamentals + Indian society/tribal studies + UPSC General Studies foundation + current-affairs discipline + Anthropology optional preparation + answer-writing ability + fieldwork/research exposure + ethics + communication + basic data/GIS skills."},{"type":"p","text":"The most important point is that Anthropology is an academic foundation and optional-subject advantage, not a guaranteed government-career pathway. Selection depends on performance in the relevant competitive examination, while the eventual career depends on the service allocated."}]}]}